{"url": "https://www.udel.edu/academics/colleges/cas/units/departments/mathematical-sciences/graduate-programs/phd-degrees/", "final_url": "https://www.udel.edu/academics/colleges/cas/units/departments/mathematical-sciences/graduate-programs/phd-degrees/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Applied Mathematics (Ph.D.) | Mathematical Sciences | College of Arts & Sciences | University of Delaware\nSkip to site content\nQuick Links\nMyUD\nMaps\nPeople Directory\nEmail\nCareers\nLibrary\nA-Z Index\nNews\nEvents\nSafety at UD\nClose\nArts & Sciences\nQuick Links\nMyUD\nMaps\nPeople Directory\nEmail\nCareers\nLibrary\nA-Z Index\nNews\nEvents\nSafety at UD\nAbout Us\nCollege Leadership\nDean's Advisory Council\nDiversity, Equity and Inclusion\nCAS Social Media\nContact Us\nProspective Students\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nTransfer Students\nVisit Us\nCurrent Students\nStudent Success Center\nStudent Scholar Programs\nAccelerated Degrees (4+1 Programs)\nCertificate Programs\nAcademics\nOur Departments\nCenters and Programs\nAssociate in Arts Program\nSecondary Education\nEnglish Language Institute\nNews & Events\nArts at UD\nAnnual Lectures and Symposia\nIn the News\nCAS Graduation Season\nResearch & Innovation\nPlastino Scholars\nResearch News & Experts\nPublications\nAlumni & Friends\nAlumni Awards\nMake A Gift\nThe Cornerstone Newsletter\nAbout Us\nCollege Leadership\nDean's Advisory Council\nDiversity, Equity and Inclusion\nCAS Social Media\nContact Us\nProspective Students\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nTransfer Students\nVisit Us\nCurrent Students\nStudent Success Center\nStudent Scholar Programs\nAccelerated Degrees (4+1 Programs)\nCertificate Programs\nAcademics\nOur Departments\nCenters and Programs\nAssociate in Arts Program\nSecondary Education\nEnglish Language Institute\nNews & Events\nArts at UD\nAnnual Lectures and Symposia\nIn the News\nCAS Graduation Season\nResearch & Innovation\nPlastino Scholars\nResearch News & Experts\nPublications\nAlumni & Friends\nAlumni Awards\nMake A Gift\nThe Cornerstone Newsletter\nUD Home\nOur Departments\nMathematical Sciences\nGraduate Programs\nPhD Degrees\nMathematical Sciences\nAbout Us\nGrants Spotlight\nSeminars and Colloquia\nSummer Programs\nGraduate Student Mathematical Modeling Camp\nSummer Math Modeling Program for High Schoolers\nReckonings Newsletter\nUndergraduate Programs\nMathematical Sciences Learning Laboratory\nFoundational Math Courses\nMath 010 \u2013 Intermediate Algebra\nMath 113 - Contemporary Mathematics\nMath 114 - Mathematics and Statistics\nMath 115 - Pre-Calculus\nMath 117 - Pre-Calculus for Scientists and Engineers\nMath 221 - Calculus\nMath 231/232 Integrated Calculus IA and IB\nMath 241 - Analytic Geometry and Calculus A\nIntermediate and Advanced Courses\nMath Placement Assessment\nMath Placement Goal by Major\nStudent Organizations\nMath Proficiency Exam\nScholarships and Awards\nCareers in Math\nCourse Offerings\nGraduate Programs\nMS Degrees\nPhD Degrees\nDual Degree MSDS & PhD\nScholarships and Awards\nGraduate Program Activities\nGraduate Student Resources\nOur Alumni\nOur People\nResearch Programs\nResources\nMake a Gift\nApply\n>\nGet More Info\n>\nRobert Coulter\nProfessor\nDirector of Graduate Programs\ncoulter@udel.edu\n(302) 831-1878\nOffice: 520 Ewing Hall\nPh.D. in Applied Mathematics or Mathematics\nThe Department of Mathematical Sciences at the University of Delaware invites applications from candidates to pursue PhD studies in Mathematics or Applied Mathematics.\nThe deadline for applications for a September 2025 start with full funding is January 15, 2025.\nApply Now\n>\nSuccessful applicants are offered a competitive package, including:\nan annual stipend of $30,000 for 9 month, with an anticipated increase in later years;\nsummer research opportunities carrying a supplement of $6,000;\nwinter and summer teaching opportunities with additional remuneration;\ninstructor of record opportunities for the best qualified students;\na route to simultaneously obtain an MS degree in Data Science at no additional cost.\nThe Department's research includes some of the most recent trends, covering a variety of areas, including analysis, computational mathematics, discrete mathematics, mathematics of data science, numerical analysis and PDE's, probability theory and its applications, and quantum information science.\nApplications must include an up-to-date CV, a personal statement, academic transcripts, three reference letters and, for international applicants, a valid TOEFL score of at least 600 points (or equivalent). GRE scores are optional.\nEnquiries are welcome by the Director of the Graduate Program, Robert Coulter at coulter@udel.edu.\nAdmission Requirements\nEach year, the deadline for spring admission is November 15 and January 15 for fall admission.\n\u200bPh.D.Admission to the Ph.D. programs in Applied Mathematics and Mathematics is open to students who have completed the equivalent of a baccalaureate degree in mathematics or related fields and who have sound preparation in linear algebra and advanced calculus. On a 4.0 system, applicants should have a GPA of at least 2.5 and an average of at least 3.0 in mathematics and related areas. Applicants who have completed an advanced degree must have done so with a GPA of at least 3.0.\nTo be eligible for admission, students from a country where English is not a primary language must demonstrate proficiency in English by meeting at least one of the following criteria:\n\u200b\u200bScore at least 600 on the paper-based TOEFL exam.\nScore at least 100 on the TOEFL iBT, with a minimum score of 20 in each section.\nScore at least 7.5 on the IELTS with a minimum score of 6.0 in each subsection.\u200b\nProgram Degree Requirements\nAn outline of the degree requirements for the Ph.D. is as follows.\nMeet the coursework requirement\nPass the Preliminary Examination requirement\nPass the Candidacy Examination\nComplete two semesters of experience in teaching undergraduate students, either as a teaching assistant or as an instructor of record.\nComplete 9 credits of MATH 969 (Doctoral Dissertation)\nComplete and successfully defend a dissertation\nOnly the coursework requirement is described below. The policy document provides more information about the remaining requirements.\nCoursework\nThere are two options for the coursework requirement: standard and accelerated.\nStandard requirement\nStudents must complete 48 credits which can come from the following sources:\n1. Any 600 level MATH course up to a maximum of 27 credits\n2. Any 800 level MATH course\n3. MATH 868 (\u201cResearch\") and MATH 870 (\u201cReading\"), up to a maximum of 12 credits combined\n4. Any 600 or 800 level non-MATH courses, up to a maximum of 6 credits.\nThese coursework requirements are a superset of those for the Master's degree which requires 30 credits. An M. S. degree is awarded once the requirements for it have been met.\nAccelerated requirement\nTo qualify for the accelerated coursework requirement, the student must successfully complete the first tier of the Preliminary Requirement before the start of the first semester (that is, by passing all required exams on the first possible date). Such an attempt at the exams counts as one of the student's regular allowed attempts. Additionally, the student must complete the second tier before the start of the third semester.\nThe accelerated course requirement is 30 credits, which can come from the following sources:\n1. Any 600 level MATH course up to a maximum of 9 credits except for MATH 600 and MATH 672. These two courses may not count towards the coursework requirement.\n2. Any 800 level MATH course\n3. MATH 868 (\u201cResearch\") and MATH 870 (\u201cReading\"), up to a maximum of 12 credits combined\n4. Any 600 or 800 level non-MATH courses, up to a maximum of 3 credits.\nRegardless of which track is taken, credit hours for which the grade is below C-minus do not count toward a graduate degree.\u200b\nCheck out our MS in Data Science\n>\nColleges\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nAbout Us\nProspective Students\nCurrent Students\nAcademics\nNews & Events\nResearch & Innovation\nAlumni & Friends\nRESOURCES\nCollege Operations\nConnect\nTOP\nUndergraduate Major Finder\nGraduate Program Finder\nPlan Your Visit\nUD Home\nEXPLORE\nAbout Us\nAthletics\nUDaily\nVirtual Tour\nEmployment\nACADEMICS\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nColleges\nLibrary\nResearch\nSERVICES\nAccessibility Notice\nPeople Directory\nMy UD\nCampus Safety\nA to Z Index\nCONNECT\nContact Us\nUniversity of Delaware Newark, DE 19716 USA\n\u00a92026 University of Delaware\nComments\nLegal Notices\nAccessibility", "links": [["Skip to site content", "https://www.udel.edu/academics/colleges/cas/units/departments/mathematical-sciences/graduate-programs/phd-degrees/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/home/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/about/visit/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/apply/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/alumni-friends/give/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/academics/colleges/cas/units/departments/mathematical-sciences/graduate-programs/phd-degrees/"], ["MyUD", "https://my.udel.edu/"], ["Maps", "http://www1.udel.edu/maps/"], ["People Directory", "http://www1.udel.edu/peoplesearch/"], ["Email", "https://www.udel.edu/content/udel/en/home/it/email"], ["Careers", "https://www.udel.edu/faculty-staff/human-resources/careers/"], ["Library", "https://library.udel.edu"], ["A-Z Index", "https://www.udel.edu/home/a-z/"], ["News", "https://www.udel.edu/udaily/"], ["Events", "https://events.udel.edu"], ["Safety at UD", "https://www.udel.edu/students/safety/"], ["Arts & Sciences", "https://www.udel.edu/content/udel/en/academics/colleges/cas"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/about/visit/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/apply/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/alumni-friends/give/"], ["", "https://www.udel.edu/academics/colleges/cas/units/department